# What the Vercel CLI must NOT upload. Without this, `vercel deploy` sweeps in large untracked
# artifacts (generated smoke outputs, media, local tooling) — a 250 MB+ upload that aborts on flaky
# networks. The web build only needs the workspace source (packages/*, apps/web, root manifests).
# Note: git-integration deploys clone the repo server-side and ignore this file; it governs CLI uploads.

# Generated / local artifacts (never in git, huge)
outputs/
.superpowers/
.claude/
.mcp.json
*.pptx
*.jpg
*.png
*.mp4
*.wav

# Docs & specs — not needed to build the web app (no package.json; safe to drop from the upload)
docs/
spec/

# Test suites are not part of the production build (the full workspace is kept so the frozen
# install still resolves — do NOT exclude packages/* or apps/*, only their tests).
**/tests/
